6. The deal state machine & the Offer Wizard (core logic — implement for real)
Model the deal as a state machine in /src/lib/deal-machine.ts with states: INTAKE → PREP → LIVE → TOURS_OFFERS → ACCEPTED → CONTRACT → IN_CONTRACT → DILIGENCE → CLEAR_TO_CLOSE → CLOSING → POST_CLOSE, plus FELL_THROUGH with a reason code. Each state owns: the next step for buyer and seller (title, body, CTA, due), the handling tasks, and the milestones rendered on both progress pages. NextStepCard, HandlingList, ProgressBar counts (e.g. 4/10) and both Timelines must all derive from this one machine — change the state, both portals update.
Offer Wizard (from Buy now or a listing CTA): 4 steps in a modal/full-page flow — (1) Terms: price, EMD $, proposed close date; (2) Financing: cash/conventional/jumbo, down %, contingency toggles (inspection, financing — note NY custom in helper text), pre-approval/proof-of-funds upload (mock, sets a "Verified funds" badge); (3) Review: full term sheet + net/certainty explainer; (4) Confirm (ConfirmDialog pattern) → Submitted state. The new offer appears instantly in Seller → Offers with an AI note generated by rule (cash+fast close → "Strongest certainty"; highest price + jumbo + long close → "Highest price is not the strongest offer — more risk and delays."; balanced → "Balanced price with standard contingencies.").
Certainty scoring (deterministic, in /src/lib/scoring.ts): cash > financed; fewer contingencies, higher EMD %, shorter close, verified funds → higher score; labels: Strongest certainty / Competitive / Highest price. Seller table and cards sort by a combined rank but display the honest note per offer.
Completing key CTAs advances the machine: e.g. buyer's "Schedule inspection" books the service and marks milestone 5's task done → buyer Home next step changes to "Review inspection report" done-state → next step becomes "Confirm attendance / await report"; keep the loop tight and visible.
